.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CHSH 1
.Os Belka
.Sh NAME
.Nm chsh
.Nd change the login shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the login shell of the named user, or of the invoking user
when no name is given.
Without
.Fl s ,
it prompts for the new shell on the controlling terminal.
An empty response leaves the current shell in place.
.Pp
A user may change their own shell after authenticating with their
password.
Both their current and new shells must be listed in
.Pa /etc/shells .
The superuser may change any account and select any executable shell.
The new shell must be an absolute path to a regular executable file.
.Pp
Updates preserve the other account fields and accounts, file ownership,
and permissions.
The password-file lock is shared with
.Xr passwd 1 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/.pwd.lock
.It Pa /etc/passwd
Account names, identifiers, home directories, and login shells.
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Account password hashes.
.It Pa /etc/shells
Permitted login shells.
.It Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
Password-file update lock.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr tcsh 1
